<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · disaster</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hurricane Mitch</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1998</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hurricane Mitch was one of the deadliest Atlantic hurricanes on record, striking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a> in late October and early November 1998. Its torrential rains caused floods and landslides that killed about 11,000 people, mostly in Honduras and Nicaragua, including some 2,000 in a mudslide on the Casita volcano. It destroyed much of the region's roads, bridges and crops, setting back the economies of Honduras and Nicaragua by years.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hurricane-mitch.jpg" alt="Hurricane Mitch" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mitch_1998-10-26_1845Z.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
